This project explores quantitative pair trading strategies between a major energy sector ETF (IQQH.DE) and its underlying constituent stocks. The analytical pipeline leverages Principal Component Analysis (PCA) for dimensionality reduction and DBSCAN clustering on correlation matrices to select the most viable candidate pairs, such as ENPH and ORSTED.CO. To predict market movements, Random Forest classifiers were implemented using multiple feature extraction methods, including raw stationary spreads, linear regression moving averages, and Relative Strength Index (RSI) momentum indicators. The strategies were rigorously backtested with a dynamic stop-loss mechanism based on 30-day local minima, demonstrating effective risk management and capital preservation during adverse market fluctuations.
